/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"Request body"},"3404":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-3","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#response-200","content":"Response 200"},"3405":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-4","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#errors","content":"Errors"},"3406":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-5","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","content":"Change a queue's settings. Omit a field to leave it as it is. `null` clears only `auto_assignment`, `max_open_per_person`, `service_levels`, `awaiting_reply` and `marked_resolved`; the last three then follow the organization's. Priorities in `service_levels` are slugs from the priority list. `service_levels` replaces both targets, so give both. A `null` resolution follows the organization's, but first response always needs a target. A queue cannot be archived or restored here. A rename is refused if another queue that is not archived has the name. Turning off automatic routing on the default queue is refused too. A rename can fail after part of it was applied; retry the same call to finish it. For administrators and queue leads."},"3407":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-6","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","content":"Omit a field to leave it as it is. Send `null` to clear `auto_assignment`, `awaiting_reply`, `marked_resolved`, `max_open_per_person`, `service_levels`. The two are different requests here, and only here. Everywhere else on this API an omitted field and a null field mean the same thing."},"3408":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-7","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#parameters","content":"| Name    | In   | Type   | Required | Description                              |\n| ------- | ---- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `queue` | path | string | yes      | The queue's id, from the list of queues. |","table":"table-0"},"3409":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-8","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"What to change on a queue. Omit a field to leave it as it is."},"3410":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-9","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field             | Type                           | Required | Description                                                                         |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `auto_assignment` | one of `least_loaded`, or null |          | How tickets are handed to operators. `null` means nobody is assigned automatically. |","table":"table-1"},"3411":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-10","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field          | Type    | Required | Description                                                                     |\n| -------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `auto_routing` | boolean |          | Whether automatic routing may send tickets here. The default queue keeps it on. |","table":"table-1"},"3412":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-11","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field            | Type            | Required | Description                                                                                                                       |\n| ---------------- | --------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `awaiting_reply` | object, or null |          | This queue's own rule for when the requester goes quiet on a ticket the agent is still handling. `null` means the organization's. |","table":"table-1"},"3413":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-12","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field            | Type           | Required | Description                                                                                   |\n| ---------------- | -------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `business_hours` | list of object |          | When this queue's clocks run. Day 0 is Monday. Empty means it keeps the organization's hours. |","table":"table-1"},"3414":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-13","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field         | Type   | Required | Description                 |\n| ------------- | ------ | -------- | --------------------------- |\n| `description` | string |          | What belongs in this queue. |","table":"table-1"},"3415":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-14","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field                 | Type    | Required | Description                                                                 |\n| --------------------- | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hold_reminder_hours` | integer |          | Hours of silence before the person a held ticket is waiting on is reminded. |","table":"table-1"},"3416":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-15","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field      | Type           | Required | Description                                                                                 |\n| ---------- | -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `holidays` | list of object |          | Holidays recorded on this queue. Service-level clocks do not skip them. Send `[]` for none. |","table":"table-1"},"3417":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-16","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field             | Type            | Required | Description                                                                  |\n| ----------------- | --------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `marked_resolved` | object, or null |          | This queue's own rule for resolved tickets. `null` means the organization's. |","table":"table-1"},"3418":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-17","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field                 | Type             | Required | Description                                                                                                                                             |\n| --------------------- | ---------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `max_open_per_person` | integer, or null |          | A recorded setting for the most open tickets one operator is handed at a time. Automatic assignment does not enforce it. `null` means none is recorded. |","table":"table-1"},"3419":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-18","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field  | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                |\n| ------ | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `name` | string |          | What this queue is called in the product. No other queue that is not archived may have it. |","table":"table-1"},"3420":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-19","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field                              | Type    | Required | Description                                                                                                   |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `restart_response_clock_on_update` | boolean |          | Whether a qualifying public comment from the responder or a queue operator restarts the first-response clock. |","table":"table-1"},"3421":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-20","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field              | Type   | Required | Description                         |\n| ------------------ | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `routing_keywords` | object |          | Words that steer automatic routing. |","table":"table-1"},"3422":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-21","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field            | Type            | Required | Description                                                                                                                                    |\n| ---------------- | --------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `service_levels` | object, or null |          | This queue's own service levels. `null` means it uses the organization's. Give both targets, as they replace the queue's service levels whole. |","table":"table-1"},"3423":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-22","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field      | Type   | Required | Description                             |\n| ---------- | ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `timezone` | string |          | The timezone its business hours are in. |","table":"table-1"},"3424":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-23","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"What happens when the requester goes quiet on a ticket the agent is still handling."},"3425":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-24","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field         | Type    | Required | Description                                                         |\n| ------------- | ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `close_hours` | integer | yes      | Hours of silence before `then` happens. More than `reminder_hours`. |","table":"table-2"},"3426":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-25","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field            | Type    | Required | Description                             |\n| ---------------- | ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `reminder_hours` | integer | yes      | Hours before the requester is reminded. |","table":"table-2"},"3427":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-26","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field  | Type                     | Required | Description                                                              |\n| ------ | ------------------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `then` | one of `cancel`, `route` | yes      | `cancel` closes the ticket out; `route` hands it to an operator instead. |","table":"table-2"},"3428":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-27","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"One window of working hours on the local week, as a request sends it. The contract writes\na request's optional `end` without null and a response's with it, so the two are separate\ncomponents."},"3429":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-28","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field | Type            | Required | Description                                                                             |\n| ----- | --------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `end` | string, or null |          | The local time the window ends, as HH:MM and not included; null for the end of the day. |","table":"table-3"},"3430":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-29","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field             | Type    | Required | Description                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `end_day_of_week` | integer | yes      | The day the window ends, the same day or later in the week. |","table":"table-3"},"3431":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-30","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field   | Type   | Required | Description                                 |\n| ------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `start` | string | yes      | The local time the window starts, as HH:MM. |","table":"table-3"},"3432":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-31","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field               | Type    | Required | Description                                              |\n| ------------------- | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `start_day_of_week` | integer | yes      | The day the window starts, 0 for Monday to 6 for Sunday. |","table":"table-3"},"3433":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-32","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"A holiday to record on a queue."},"3434":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-33","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field  | Type   | Required | Description                      |\n| ------ | ------ | -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `date` | string | yes      | The calendar day, as YYYY-MM-DD. |","table":"table-4"},"3435":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-34","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field  | Type   | Required | Description             |\n| ------ | ------ | -------- | ----------------------- |\n| `name` | string | yes      | What the day is called. |","table":"table-4"},"3436":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-35","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"What happens to a ticket in this queue that sits in `resolved`."},"3437":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-36","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field              | Type    | Required | Description                                                 |\n| ------------------ | ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `auto_close_hours` | integer | yes      | Hours without activity before the ticket closes on its own. |","table":"table-5"},"3438":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-37","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"New routing keywords. Omit a list to leave it as it is."},"3439":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-38","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field     | Type           | Required | Description                                                                                                                            |\n| --------- | -------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `exclude` | list of string |          | Tickets mentioning these are kept out of this queue. If every queue is kept out, all of them are considered again. Send `[]` for none. |","table":"table-6"},"3440":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-39","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field     | Type           | Required | Description                                                                             |\n| --------- | -------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `include` | list of string |          | A hint: tickets mentioning these are more likely to be routed here. Send `[]` for none. |","table":"table-6"},"3441":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-40","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"The service levels a queue keeps instead of the organization's. They replace both targets,\nso give both; read the queue first to keep the one you are not changing."},"3442":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update-41","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/queues-update#request-body","content":"| Field            | Type   | Required | Description                                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------- | ------ | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------