pi/2026-09-14/tickets-followers-add","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-followers-add#response-200","content":"| Field   | Type            | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| ------- | --------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `state` | string, or null |          | Slug of the state this ticket is in. A new ticket has none until routing opens it; the response that files it shows `open` ahead of that. Routing can still move it, and a ticket that routing could not open stays without one, so get the ticket again to see where it settled. |","table":"table-2"},"3956":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-followers-add-23","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-followers-add","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-followers-add#response-200","content":"| Field         | Type            | Required | Description                                                                                                                        |\n| ------------- | --------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `synced_from` | string, or null |          | The other system this ticket is linked to. Known values: `freshservice`, `jira`, `servicenow`; `external` for a system not listed. |","table":"table-2"},"3957":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-followers-add-24","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/tickets-followers-add