------ | --------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `message` | string, or null | yes      | What the workflow said. `null` when it said nothing. |","table":"table-2"},"5188":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-23","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field    | Type                       | Required | Description                                              |\n| -------- | -------------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | one of `SUCCESS`, `FAILED` | yes      | `SUCCESS` or `FAILED`, as the workflow's author decided. |","table":"table-2"},"5189":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-24","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"Why a run failed."},"5190":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-25","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field  | Type                                                                                                  | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `code` | one of `auth`, `validation`, `transient`, `permanent`, `unclassified`, `business`, `system` or string | yes      | The kind of failure: `auth` is a sign-in or permission problem, `validation` is input that was refused, `transient` is a problem that may pass, `permanent` is one that will not, `business` is a rule of the workflow, `system` is a fault on our side and `unclassified` is any other. |","table":"table-3"},"5191":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-26","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field     | Type   | Required | Description                            |\n| --------- | ------ | -------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `message` | string | yes      | What went wrong, for a person to read. |","table":"table-3"},"5192":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-27","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field       | Type             | Required | Description                                                                |\n| ----------- | ---------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `retryable` | boolean, or null | yes      | Whether starting the same run again can work. `null` when it is not known. |","table":"table-3"},"5193":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-28","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field    | Type                                                       | Required | Description                                                        |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `source` | one of `action`, `workflow`, `runtime`, `system` or string | yes      | Whether an action, the workflow, the runtime or the system failed. |","table":"table-3"},"5194":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-29","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"An approval, task or form the run is waiting on."},"5195":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-30","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field     | Type    | Required | Description                |\n| --------- | ------- | -------- | -------------------------- |\n| `can_act` | boolean | yes      | Whether you can answer it. |","table":"table-4"},"5196":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-31","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field | Type   | Required | Description                            |\n| ----- | ------ | -------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `id`  | string | yes      | The request's id, as approvals use it. |","table":"table-4"},"5197":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-32","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field  | Type                                        | Required | Description                   |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `kind` | one of `approval`, `task`, `form` or string | yes      | `approval`, `task` or `form`. |","table":"table-4"},"5198":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-33","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field    | Type   | Required | Description       |\n| -------- | ------ | -------- | ----------------- |\n| `prompt` | string | yes      | What it asks for. |","table":"table-4"},"5199":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-34","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"What can be done about a failed run."},"5200":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-35","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field     | Type   | Required | Description                       |\n| --------- | ------ | -------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `message` | string | yes      | What to do, for a person to read. |","table":"table-5"},"5201":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-36","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field  | Type                                                                                | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `type` | one of `connect_provider`, `select_connection`, `retry`, `manual`, `none` or string | yes      | `connect_provider` means a service has to be connected again, `select_connection` means a choice between connected accounts is needed, `retry` means the same run can be started again, `manual` means a person has to fix it, and `none` means nothing helps. |","table":"table-5"},"5202":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-37","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"How a finished run ended."},"5203":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-38","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field         | Type                        | Required | Description                                                               |\n| ------------- | --------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `finished_at` | string (date-time), or null | yes      | When it finished. `null` for runs that finished before this was recorded. |","table":"table-6"},"5204":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-39","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field     | Type                                                                            | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `outcome` | one of `succeeded`, `failed`, `canceled`, `abandoned`, `wait_expired` or string | yes      | `succeeded`, `failed`, `canceled`, `abandoned` or `wait_expired`. `abandoned` means the run could not be followed to an end, and `wait_expired` that it waited for a person or an outside event until the wait ran out. Other outcomes can be added, so a value not listed here is not an error. |","table":"table-6"},"5205":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-40","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"The ticket a run belongs to."},"5206":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-41","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#response-200","content":"| Field | Type   | Required | Description                              |\n| ----- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `id`  | string | yes      | The ticket id people see in the product. |","table":"table-7"},"5207":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-42","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#errors","content":"A failed call answers with a problem body: a stable `code` to branch on, a `detail` for people, and `retryable`, which is advice for that one response."},"5208":{"id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get-43","page_id":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/2026-09-14/workflows-runs-get#errors","content":"| Code                            | HTTP status | Meaning                                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------- | ----------- | -------------------------------------------