d it another way, such as by working its queue. Removing someone else also makes you a follower of the ticket."},"9437":{"id":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove-6","page_id":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove#parameters","content":"| Name     | In   | Type   | Required | Description                                                  |\n| -------- | ---- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `ticket` | path | string | yes      | The ticket id people see in the product, such as `ACME-042`. |","table":"table-0"},"9438":{"id":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove-7","page_id":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove#request-body","content":"Who to remove from a ticket's followers."},"9439":{"id":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove-8","page_id":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove#request-body","content":"| Field    | Type           | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| -------- | -------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `emails` | list of string |          | People to remove, by their email address. Each must be a member of this organization. Use this when you don't have their id. `people` and `emails` can be sent together, and one request can name at most 100 people counting both. |","table":"table-1"},"9440":{"id":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove-9","page_id":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove#request-body","content":"| Field    | Type                  | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |\n| -------- | --------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `people` | list of string (uuid) |          | People to remove, by their stable id. Anyone can remove themselves. Removing someone else needs you to work this ticket's queue. The requester and the assignee can't be removed. One request can name at most 100 people, counting `people` and `emails`. |","table":"table-1"},"9441":{"id":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove-10","page_id":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove#response-200","content":"| Field      | Type            | Required | Description           |\n| ---------- | --------------- | -------- | --------------------- |\n| `assignee` | object, or null |          | Who is working on it. |","table":"table-2"},"9442":{"id":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove-11","page_id":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/latest/tickets-followers-remove#response-200","content":"| Field               | Type            | Required | Description                             |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `available_actions` | object, or null |          | What this caller