ch as Ask chat self-service in a workflow's access settings in the app. Turn it on and everyone in your organization can start the workflow themselves, as themselves, for example from Ask. Turning it on gives everyone in your organization the right to start the workflow. Turning it off leaves that right in place but unused, so turning it on again is one step. To turn it on, the workflow must be published and its inputs must work for people starting it themselves, or it is refused and nothing is changed. Turning it off is always allowed. A workflow that is turned off takes no new runs, whether or not this is on. The reply shows the workflow as it is now."},"10094":{"id":"/docs/api/latest/workflows-availability-set-6","page_id":"/docs/api/latest/workflows-availability-set","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/latest/workflows-availability-set#parameters","content":"| Name       | In   | Type   | Required | Description                                    |\n| ---------- | ---- | ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `workflow` | path | string | yes      | The workflow's id, from the list of workflows. |","table":"table-0"},"10095":{"id":"/docs/api/latest/workflows-availability-set-7","page_id":"/docs/api/latest/workflows-availability-set","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/latest/workflows-availability-set#request-body","content":"Whether to offer a workflow to everyone in the organization to start themselves."},"10096":{"id":"/docs/api/latest/workflows-availability-set-8","page_id":"/docs/api/latest/workflows-availability-set","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/api/latest/workflows-availability-set#request-body","content":"| Field              | Type    | Required | Description                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------ | ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------